WEBVTT

00:08:58.836 --> 00:09:00.196
And I can't prove it,

00:09:00.236 --> 00:09:03.196
but I know it was because I didn't
plan the Christmas party."

00:09:03.236 --> 00:09:05.116
So there's also this expectation

00:09:05.116 --> 00:09:08.036
when we don't do
that unpaid labor at work,

00:09:08.076 --> 00:09:10.996
that we're not productive,
that we're not committed.

00:09:11.036 --> 00:09:14.316
You know, so I think really
having a conversation

00:09:14.316 --> 00:09:18.156
about how we value
that labor is critical.

00:09:18.156 --> 00:09:21.756
WPR: One TED Member asks,
“If it’s a buyer’s market for employees,

00:09:21.796 --> 00:09:24.116
what do you think women
should ask for first

00:09:24.156 --> 00:09:26.836
from their employers
when it comes to to better benefits?

00:09:26.876 --> 00:09:28.556
Is there one sticking thing

00:09:28.596 --> 00:09:31.476
that you think really
we should be focusing on?"